Original commit body from b64849a:

Add tree-sitter based analyzer for Common Lisp (.lisp, .lsp, .cl, .asd files).

Detects:
- defun, defmacro, defmethod, defgeneric (functions)
- defclass, defstruct (types)
- defvar, defparameter, defconstant (variables)
- defpackage (packages)
- Function call edges with cross-file resolution
- use-package import edges

Key design decisions:
- Handles both lowercase (defun) and uppercase (DEFUN) forms since
  tree-sitter-commonlisp only creates defun nodes for lowercase
- Supports keyword syntax for package names (:myapp vs myapp)
- Case-insensitive name handling (CL is case-insensitive by default)
